---
description: Frontend Development Code Guidelines
globs: 
alwaysApply: false
---
- When writing frontend code, prioritize using Next.js as the framework
- Prefer the combination of shadcn/ui and Tailwind(v4) CSS for UI components, Zustand state management.
- Do not use Next.js API routes (/api); always use backend APIs for all API requests
- Use ts instead of js.
- The ultimate expression of "less is more"
- Consistency trumps individuality.
- Adopt the Progressive Disclosure principle. Try to avoid implementing all the functions at once. Functions can be suspended or elegantly reveal the hidden functions when needed.
- The Power of White Space
- When it comes to user experience, it is advisable to choose "Load First, Navigate Later".
- If the backend API is unclear or in question, use the MCP api docs tool to find the relevant API definition- 
- The UI library should be isolated from the code base and placed in components/ui
- Try to ensure that the versions of react and next are not changed
- **🌙 MANDATORY Dark Mode Compliance**: Every new component, feature, or UI change MUST be tested and optimized for dark mode. Always use semantic color tokens from globals.css, never hardcode colors. Verify WCAG AA contrast ratios in both light and dark themes before committing.
- **🎨 Visual Hierarchy Validation**: All UI cha enges must maintain clear visual separation between background layers (main → sidebar → cards → interactive elements). Test readability across different lighting conditions.
- Finally, it is necessary to ensure that make frontend-all passes
